A||N||8||FieroGTguy||Please Help With Diagnosis||||1||
Z||000000||FieroGTguy||11-28-2001||02:59 PM||||I just bought a GT with a new 3.1 Jasper engine installed by IRM.  The only problem that I bought it with was an EGR problem.  I replaced the EGR pipe, and still get the code 32 and poor gas mileage.  What is my next step to fix?<P>That was my warming up question...  Here is my larger problem that is driving me crazy.  After start-up, the engine has an unstable idle and fluxes between 1000-2000 RPM.  But the major problem on a cold engine is on the take-off in first and second gear.  Once the clutch engages, the car goes a few feet then wants to stall (bucks).  It does the same in second gear.  I give it more gas not to stall, then it takes off.  The problem goes away after the first 10 take-offs, or the first 5min.  I am clueless where to begin.<P>Any/all help would be much appreciated!<P>Thanks,<BR>Greg||||reg||1
Z||000001||My7Fieros||11-28-2001||03:11 PM||||You replaced the EGR tube, did you replace the EGR itself? (The round brass thing just s/o the dist).<BR>Idle prob...hmmm, IAC, throttle position, maybe.<BR>As far as the wanting to stall at first in 1 and 2 gears, my 86 SE does that to on cold starts. I usually let her run for a couple of minutes until it idles down before going, then I dont have that prob.||||reg||1
Z||000002||California Kid||11-28-2001||03:19 PM||||This could be the problem because it will cause the same symptoms. Inside the throttle body there is a port that can become completely blocked with carbon deposits, the port is about the diameter of a pencil. Even if it isn't the problem it will improve the engine performance.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/californiakidsig_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||lou||11-28-2001||04:53 PM||||I would guess that it is the tps ( throttle position sensor ).  Either it is not adjusted properly or just bad.<p>[This message has been edited by lou (edited 11-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||11-28-2001||06:21 PM||||FieroGTguy - with a code 32, did you replace the EGR tube? (runs from the EGR valve to the plenum) - more than likely it is the EGR selenoid itself (right side of the plenum just below the thermostat housing - vacuum lines plug into it) ...... Also, a surge of 1000 RPM could be from a vacuum leak (also EGR related) -- try correcting the EGR problem and see if the surging takes care of itself in the same fix.<p>[This message has been edited by tgowens (edited 11-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||watts||11-28-2001||07:43 PM||||I agree with the above.  Replace (or at least check) the EGR solenoid.  The ECM has no way of knowing if the EGR valve is ever open or closed...  just if the vaccum signal has been applied to it or not.<BR><P>------------------<BR>87/88 V6 5spd Notchback Hybrid<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/watts_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroGTguy||11-28-2001||07:48 PM||||Thank you for immediate responses.  This forum is great.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I'll check the EGR solenoid and the EGR itself, and post progress.<P>Greg||||reg||1
Z||000007||87GTZ34||11-28-2001||10:13 PM||||I agree w/ My7 on this.  It sounds like the valve itself is leaking vacuum through the diaphram.  GL||||reg||1
Z||000008||ka4nkf||11-29-2001||09:10 PM||||Also check the IAC sensor this will make it have an eratic idle.||||reg||1
